export anchor TelegraphOfficeStyle:
    number: 399
    screen: EmailClient
    name: Telegraph office
    idea: Mail as a sepia telegraph counter, with folders as brass plaques carrying morse marks, the inbox as a numbered received book, and the open message typed onto a telegram form.
    base: dark
    palette:
        umber: #1c150f, the page and fields
        counter: #261d15, the header sign, the ledger and the style sheet
        form: #2f241a, the telegram and the open ledger entry
        groove: #47372a, ruled lines and borders
        cream: #f0e3c9, text
        sepia: #c3ae8c, subjects, box labels and meta
        brass: #d6aa5c, plaques, morse lines, the primary key and the open entry bar
        brassHigh: #f0cd88, the lit plaque top, focus and Starred
        brassLow: #8a6a33, the telegram frame and key edges
        onBrass: #241703, text on brass
        oxblood: #e48a76, the New mark with its filled dot
        wire: #9fc4b8, the Encl. mark
    type:
        A slab stack, Rockwell, Rockwell Nova, Roboto Slab, DejaVu Serif,
        Georgia, at a 15px base for names and headings. The sign is 26px
        caps tracked wide, the telegram subject 24px at 700, senders 16px,
        bold when unread. A typewriter stack, American Typewriter, Courier
        Prime, Courier New, sets subjects, times, marks and the telegram
        body at 17px with 1.8 leading on faint ruled lines.
    layout:
        A sign across the top holds a small drawn brass telegraph key on a
        wooden base, Brightwork Mail in wide caps over Telegraph office,
        Mara Okafor, and a boxed field reading Search the book, all above a
        double rule. Three columns follow. The left, Pigeon rack, stacks
        the folders as small brass toned plaques, each with the name, the
        count for Inbox 12 and Drafts 2, and a line of decorative morse
        marks under it. Inbox is lit in bright brass. Labels follow in the
        same plaques. The middle, Received book, Inbox, is a framed ledger
        with three ruled columns, the entry number, the time and a cell with
        the sender, the subject with its quoted snippet in typewriter, and
        boxed marks. Entry 1 is shaded with a brass bar. The right column
        is a telegram form in a brass frame with an offset outline, a band
        reading TELEGRAM with No. 1, received, Clients, three boxes for
        From, To and Time sent, the subject in slab, the body typed with a
        small STOP after each sentence, a line of decorative morse, and
        pill shaped brass keys with a hard shadow, Reply lit. Below 1100px
        the telegram moves under the book. On a phone the book comes first,
        then the telegram, then the plaques two by two.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between the columns, 10px ledger cells, 18px telegram padding.
    density: Medium. A ruled six entry book beside a full telegram.
    corners: Nearly square at 2 to 3px. Only the brass keys are pill shaped.
    borders: 2px groove frames, 1px ruled cells, a 4px double rule under the sign, a brass frame with an offset outline on the telegram.
    shadows: A hard 3px dark drop under each key so it looks pressable, and gradients on brass.
    icons:
        A drawn brass key in the sign. Marks are typographic in thin boxes,
        a filled dot plus New, a star plus Starred, a plus sign plus Encl.,
        and a dotted box for labels. Morse lines are decoration only.
    focus: A 2px bright brass outline offset 3px plus a soft brass halo.
    tone: Period office words, such as Received book, Pigeon rack, Time sent and STOP.
